<title>USA: Bancrofts support Dow Jones independence - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Bancrofts support Dow Jones independence - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The family with a controlling interest in Dow Jones &amp; Co has issued a statement that they are unanimously committed to maintaining the company's independence, the electronic version of the Wall Street Journal said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The paper said the statement was signed by the four members of the Bancroft family who sit on the Dow Jones board and sent to Fortune magazine.</p>
<p>Recent reports have speculated that competitors, including Reuters Holdings Plc, have expressed interest in buying, merging or forming a joint venture with Dow Jones.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
